{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon","id":199366,"title":"Why can't the God-Machine recapture a freshly fallen demon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-16T16:14:00-07:00","id":199366,"title":"Why can't the God-Machine recapture a freshly fallen demon?","content":"One question has been bugging me: Why can't the God-Machine easily recapture a freshly fallen demon?<br /> <br /> It seems that in the minutes after she Falls, a demon is extremely vulnerable. She has only the Cover she &quot;rode in on&quot;, and she is either exactly where she was when she Fell, or she's, at most, a short distance away. Some new demons presumably get scooped up right away, but enough stay on the run for this game to exist. So how does that happen?<br /> <br /> Doesn't the Machine know the last position of the angel that just went dark? Doesn't it know exactly what Cover the demon has? Why can't it immediately send agents to search for that Cover?<br /> <br /> I keep rereading the parts that talk about the first cover a demon acquires, the one that is a remnant of her former angelic mission, but the only relevant information they give is that the demon writes their current angelic Cover into the fabric of the world and cuts itself off from direct contact with the machine. OK, so, translation: the demon winks off the grid with only the angelic disguise it possessed at the time. One passage reads:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons can pass as human almost effortlessly. Even angels are usually hard-pressed to recognize a demon shrouded by her Cover. There are a thousand ways, however, that an infiltration can fail, from the demonic infiltrator accidentally giving herself away to a particularly paranoid angel\u2019s routine etheric scans of his<br /> employees. </div> </div> </div>which seems to suggest that angels can't easily sniff out who is a demon. But can't they be told exactly what Cover the angel was using right when she vanished?<br /> <br /> I thought of some possible answers, though I'd prefer some canonical support. Possible answer #1: Since angels are basically specialized programs extending from the Machine itself, the Fall involves not only writing themselves into the world but also <i>writing themselves out of the God-Machine </i>to a certain extent. They essentially seal up the gap left by their absence, tying up loose ends. So the Machine has some lingering references to the demon, enough to know it went missing, but has trouble conveying the identity of the demon, because it lacks a complete description of her Cover.<br /> <br /> Or, the Machine remembers exactly who went missing and how they could be recognized, and the only thing keeping new demons from being immediately recaptured is the brief window of time between the Fall and the arrival of the first demon-hunting angels or other Machine agents. In that time, the demon has to have scrammed. But then I just go back to thinking, why can't the angels just target the Cover--the person's records, family, address--directly?<br /> <br /> Or maybe they do, and what I'm calling a point of mystery is actually, you know, the whole game, as written.<br /> <br /> Help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":".  Adding tags 07-16-2014, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:59:35-07:00","id":199417,"title":"","content":"I'd say the G-M can't recall the identity of the Cover. Or even people. To it, we're not &quot;Dr. John Smith of the London Smiths&quot;, we're &quot;Generic Organics Repair Unit Class-Gamma-3; 7/9&quot; or some such other designation.<br /> <br /> This is relevant because, cannonically when an Angel falls, there can be an Aetheric disturbance; (Opening fiction: Enemy Action). I imagine it is like a burst of static in the middle of a radio broadcast, it causes what appears to be a lot of interference. Afterwards, when you can hear the song again, how long does it take you to notice that one of the backup singers isn't there? Which one is identified by a process of elimination, ('Sound off').<br /> <br /> Tracking down the errant resource is that much harder though, because the rest of the world because it only bothers to learn the designation relevant to it's requirements It might be a bit of a stretch, but I think the Angels fill in the 'gaps' in their Covers as required. The G-M doesn't care. Which means it doesn't keep track of such irrelevant junk data.. It knows it is looking for a Doctor with a certain level of clearance at Hospital A, but Dr. Smith is one of many. 7 of 9 in my example above. With this in mind, they don't need to go to the point of &quot;<i>writing themselves out of the God-Machine </i>&quot;, at least not entirely. Once the G-M loses that '7/9', it only has a description. Add the time required to unleash the hounds &amp; transit, even the most disoriented newly Unchained will have moved on, minus the most damaged of Integrators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:03:17-07:00","id":199423,"title":"","content":"A Cover isn't a dossier with a bunch of fake IDs attached; it's a piece of supernatural Infrastructure that hides an angel and creates a space for it to occupy in reality. Once the angel goes rogue with the infrastructure attached, that piece of Concealment Infrastructure is now working against the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:04:39-07:00","id":199426,"title":"","content":"Your first explanation is the most common one. The first thing a demon does when it Falls is to wipe as many records of its existence out of the God-Machine's memory as it can. FallenEco's works well too and is along the same lines I suppose one could botch that job and be forced to find a new Cover real quick (which could make for an interesting story in itself), but the general assumption is that a demon in its first flesh isn't an angry red dot on the God-Machine's radar. Partially this is because it seems like a former angel would know better than to leave an obvious path to its door, but mostly it's because there are soooo many story possibilities for a newly Fallen demon who is still in its last Cover as an angel, and it would be a shame to cut off those opportunities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:13:50-07:00","id":199445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=199417#post199417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it is like a burst of static in the middle of a radio broadcast, it causes what appears to be a lot of interference. Afterwards, when you can hear the song again, how long does it take you to notice that one of the backup singers isn't there? Which one is identified by a process of elimination, ('Sound off').</div> </div> </div> </div>The backup singers analogy is great. And yeah, I can see how the GM only cares about certain parameters and results, not the specifics of the tools it sends to do those things. I suppose there is even precedence for it to have &quot;bad records&quot;, since it makes mistakes that sometimes results in impossible missions or contradictory ones.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your reply.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:17:19-07:00","id":199447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=199426#post199426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the general assumption is that a demon in its first flesh isn't an angry red dot on the God-Machine's radar. Partially this is because it seems like a former angel would know better than to leave an obvious path to its door, but mostly it's because there are soooo many story possibilities for a newly Fallen demon who is still in its last Cover as an angel, and it would be a shame to cut off those opportunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I definitely was operating under the assumption that the demon should be able to keep its first Cover, since having to do away with it at shortly after character creation spoils story possibilities not to mention the player's initial character concept.<br /> <br /> Thanks, people. All this makes sense to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:28:37-07:00","id":199493,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember what the God Machine is, and the God Machine isn't.<br /> <br /> It's easy to fall into the trap of viewing the God Machine as a huge, monolithic intelligence agency.<br /> <br /> It's not, though. The God Machine can't reduce itself to the level of an intelligence agency. It doesn't have a central hub or repository of information, like the FBI or CIA might. It doesn't really occur to the God Machine why it would even need something like that. The God Machine can't relate to tiny little souls well enough to understand why those kind of tools would be useful.<br /> <br /> So, when the God Machine acts, it's not doing so like the NSA would. It doesn't have a 'Most Wanted' list, and it doesn't really keep careful track of where individual angels are (or where they fall). It's concerned with much more big picture issues, possibly extending outside of one particular dimension and one particular timeline.<br /> <br /> It acts out of reflex - like a sneeze. When you are provoked to sneeze, you're not really aware of what's irritating you. You aren't actually envisioning the particle in your nose that's making you feel like you have to sneeze. You just do it. When you sneeze, your body puts into place a sequence of autonomous processes that are more-or-less effective at resolving the issue.<br /> <br /> So it is with the God Machine. It's tempting to assume the God Machine 'remembers' particular angels, or Unchained, that is has them in a 'database'... a GODNET, if you will, that all angels and God Machine loyal enterprises can access. This is, in my opinion, a bad way of running the game because it shuts down quite a lot of fun for players.<br /> <br /> The God Machine may sneeze out something that'll make an effort to remember the Unchained... maybe an Angel, that starts collecting a database and starts trying to track people down... but that sneeze exists in isolation from all the other sneezes. It doesn't have omniescent access to everything the God Machine knows. The sneeze doesn't 'report back' to an ever-growing storehouse of information that's designed to ferret out demons; one day, the sneeze will just end, until another sneeze emerges.<br /> <br /> When an Unchained escapes, it's a similar situation. Unchained running away don't really provoke sneezes. You might imagine they would... if you were running a company, or an intelligence agency, and a well-trained asset vanishes?... you notice. But, in point of fact, the God Machine just doesn't really care. After all, that's what angels are for.<br /> <br /> Some angels find this ineffeciency very frustrating, but that's when the God Machine just says : haters gonna hate. The system works. Sneezes more or less keep the nose clear, even if a cell by cell census is not available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 07-16-2014, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:31:04-07:00","id":199557,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply. I find your post quite helpful and interesting. There are some parts of it, however, that feel to me like an interpretation possibly not supported by the GMC book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=199493#post199493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is with the God Machine. It's tempting to assume the God Machine 'remembers' particular angels, or Unchained, that is has them in a 'database'... a GODNET, if you will, that all angels and God Machine loyal enterprises can access. This is, in my opinion, a bad way of running the game because it shuts down quite a lot of fun for players.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my understanding that part of what demons lose when they Fall is access to some kind of information network. This loss is put forth as the reason they cannot immediately remember all the embeds that exist. Angels are said to have a much bigger picture that they simply don't question or pay attention to. I seem to recall some fiction from the POV of pre-fallen angels who reach out with heightened information receptors and sense faraway angels and gain updating intel about their mission. There are also sites of command/control:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The God-Machine is a machine, and any machine as complex as it is has parts that are responsible for setting the overall strategy of the God-Machine. The God-Machine needs some means of gathering information and making decisions \u2014 the equivalent of a command and control center or central processing unit. p35 </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, I don't think all loyalist agents should be able to tap into a phone jack and gain access to the Motherboard. I also realize that the Machine is slow, has a million pots on the stove, and is not immune to error or insanity. But on the other hand, it is established that it puts immense resources into angel creation--so much that it recycles them, so I don't think it's too much to expect it to track where each one is with some effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 07-16-2014, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T20:10:41-07:00","id":199573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=199557#post199557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's too much to expect it to track where each one is with some effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are angels whose jobs include space exploration and leading battles against alien armies.<br /> <br /> There are angels whose jobs include pretending to be a specific person for decades at a time.<br /> <br /> There are angels whose jobs amount to distracting a single person for the span of four seconds.<br /> <br /> None of these angels exist in a vaccuum; all of them require Infrastructure in the form of occult matrices, cultists, sacred geometry, or other nonsense that is not other angels, and the degree of oversight needed to immediately track an angel is at odds with the number of missions angels are given where they appear to be handed their orders and then left to their own devices between briefings and debriefings.<br /> <br /> God is specifically capable of getting stuck in logic loops that It doesn't attempt to terminate until they're brought to Its attention - that's how most Suborned Infrastructure works, in fact - and It's constantly juggling It-knows-how-many projects at once while trying to account for interference from demons and Its own blind spots regarding humanity and other supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> The Machine, insofar as comparing it to a discrete entity is wise, is one big guy with the cosmic account-book trying to make the numbers add up with the minimum of fuss while simultaneously running riot over a bunch of unruly children who don't know that an experiment is at work and a smaller bunch of little guys trying to steal his funding, abscond with the kids, or kick him out of the building.<br /> <br /> This is a being that is practically defined by the principle of least action. Most individual angels don't Fall with vital irreplaceable resources that wouldn't be as easily regained by reclaiming any other Unchained, and the commitments required to keep perfect backups of all the data the Machine deals with from moment to moment is almost certainly more than it would be worth to simply set about rerecording lost data; I wouldn't be surprised if a lot of Falls were concealed under the metaphysical equivalent of &quot;lost three pages of document reencryption key due to power outage, will recover when Deadlines A, 12, and \u00dfiv are not looming in the immediate vicinity.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:36:45-07:00","id":199801,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I believe the book says somewhere that when an angel falls the GM immediately loses track of the cover, so a demon could stay theoretically in that same original cover for decades without running any greater risk than a demon who immediately changes cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:50:08-07:00","id":200249,"title":"","content":"Think of G-M as a decentralized computing system, rather than an individual in the classic sense. It is a hive mind, gestalt of all its nodes. To respond on individual human level, the G-M developed Angel class machines. When such machine has to be deployed into reality, it is connected to the Cover class machines and any other resources it might need for its mission.<br /> When Angel falls, the disconnection sends shock-waves through the system, disconnecting out the machines that were connected to it. Including the Cover ones.<br /> The G-M does not remember the cover, because it was cut out from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:58:43-07:00","id":200256,"title":"","content":"The assumption I've run with is that the Machine loses track of the cover. In the metaphysical short-circuit that is the Fall, it's like that data gets scorched out of it's accessible information, and like Satchel and others have said, it's operating on the principle of least action and juggling an impossibly large amount of projects. Between those two things, a Demon doing nothing but living his Cover for years might not run into any problems. Unfortunately most Demons don't seem to like to do nothing ;P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T15:45:12-07:00","id":200451,"title":"","content":"Also remember the reason the machine makes angels in the first place: it's phenomenally powerful, but is almost incapable of comprehending or acting on things in an individual scope. Thinking in terms of a discrete being is hard, if not impossible for it. That's why it needs to create discrete servants with a capacity for will of their own.<br /> <br /> The God Machine is the embodiment of the principle of least action, but its also the embodiment of acting on the big picture. Focusing down on just one fallen demon is likely both outside the scope of it's effort when it first happens as well as potentially just not within it's power to do. Hence creating servants to specifically do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1097,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","user":"underwoodfive","date":". 07-18-2014, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T16:02:13-07:00","id":200480,"title":"","content":"okay i feel like i need to reiterate what &quot;principle of least action&quot; means before it gets reduced to a forum buzzword:<br /> <br /> it means &quot;the universe is lazy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T20:19:04-07:00","id":200674,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Alternately, the G-M <i>does</i> capture a significant portion of the newly Fallen. The ones that escape are the few who are tough, clever, adaptable and above all else <i>lucky</i>.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 07-19-2014, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:33:45-07:00","id":200711,"title":"","content":"To bring up one more option. Maybe the fall happens before their part of the system was activated. I mean if the objective was to keep a person alive until noon on the 17th of October next year and the Fallen gets tired of the person and leaves a year early even if the GM was keeping tabs on that project enough to know who was there the Fallen in question has a year before the job would be over and unless the person dies before then it's unlikely that angel would be noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T13:50:56-07:00","id":201431,"title":"","content":"All helpful posts. I believe my question has been adequately answered, though I would welcome further input.<br /> <br /> I do, however, feel the need to stress that I understood that the Machine is &quot;lazy&quot; and needs angels to operate at the level of individuals, but my point was that since it *does* have angels working for it, why don't they instantly know exactly who their target is? Some of the above posters have given quite useful answers, but IMO one cannot answer the question without addressing why those angels don't have the necessary info (or if they do, why they can't complete their job with maximum efficiency.) The Machine could be as decentralized as you like, but it still clearly has a purpose/purposes, and it clearly wants to recover (almost) all demons, or else it wouldn't send angels to find them. Presumably, no matter where a demon ends up in the world, there are angels nearby who become alerted to its Fall and begin chasing it. Therefore, in most cases, the Machine is centralized enough that it can direct angels to begin the hunt. It puzzled me that these angels might be tasked with the recovery of a demon without having enough information to go, &quot;There it is.&quot;<br /> <br /> Same with laziness. You can make the Machine as lazy (methodical, preoccupied) as you like, but AFAIK, demons are on the run *immediately*, so it seems evident that the Machine does not wait around very long to give the hunt signal.<br /> <br /> All that having been said, I do see how the points raised above can contribute to just enough wiggle room for some demons to evade capture, and like some said above, I think one has to assume that either the fall disrupts the Machine's &quot;memory&quot; of the Cover, or the Cover is only known to the Machine in vague terms. This latter option is fine, I suppose, but it stretches the imagination, considering that demons are an ongoing problem for the Machine, and it seems that the methodical, efficient way to solve it would be to f_cking take better notes about who is who! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T18:10:34-07:00","id":201667,"title":"","content":"Not all Falls are created equal. Its easy to imagine it as a routine, since its what generates largely equal characters. But every project is different even in a Being that seeks uniformity. Some demons are in the wrong or right place when they fall--a HK unit who abruptly falls with his two companions next to him is less likely to evade his pursuers than the single angel installed over some small side project. Likewise, the cover could easily come into the picture: if a president was an angel and it fell, GM would intervene BEFORE it happened. But if it was a mysterious secret service agent with little background and a generic name, he could get away before a human, angel, program, or machine to even notice. Some demons fall to the sounds of sky trumpets and immediately take off running. Another's fall is so subtle, he continues the conversation with his angelic partner without any suspicion before he slips away &quot;to finish his mission&quot; and promptly drops off the radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T18:42:10-07:00","id":201674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=201431#post201431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do, however, feel the need to stress that I understood that the Machine is &quot;lazy&quot; and needs angels to operate at the level of individuals, but my point was that since it *does* have angels working for it, why don't they instantly know exactly who their target is? Some of the above posters have given quite useful answers, but IMO one cannot answer the question without addressing why those angels don't have the necessary info (or if they do, why they can't complete their job with maximum efficiency.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because time and other resources are not perfectly efficiently leveraged - Aether is just the most common demonstration of this principle - and the Machine is big-picture enough that without being flagged as significant little details can slip through (and &quot;little&quot; can be fairly big when talking about a Machine spread across multiple portions of the material realm).<br /> <br /> There's a coin in the Quickstart that has blatant angelic script <i>because of time-constraints.</i> The infernal engine is not run by Laplace's Demon, who sees all things and can perfectly describe them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same with laziness. You can make the Machine as lazy (methodical, preoccupied) as you like, but AFAIK, demons are on the run *immediately*, so it seems evident that the Machine does not wait around very long to give the hunt signal. </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, you're cut off from the channels of information that can immediately tell you how much the enemy knows and thus must assume that they are acting <i>right now</i> so that you can negate as much advantage as any pursuers might have over you.<br /> <br /> Streisand Effect or no, initiating your coverup of your Cover's disconnection immediately gives you known variables to work with - what you did to cover it up - and a trail you can mess with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T22:03:52-07:00","id":201781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=201431#post201431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All helpful posts. I believe my question has been adequately answered, though I would welcome further input.<br /> <br /> I do, however, feel the need to stress that I understood that the Machine is &quot;lazy&quot; and needs angels to operate at the level of individuals, but my point was that since it *does* have angels working for it, why don't they instantly know exactly who their target is? Some of the above posters have given quite useful answers, but IMO one cannot answer the question without addressing why those angels don't have the necessary info (or if they do, why they can't complete their job with maximum efficiency.) The Machine could be as decentralized as you like, but it still clearly has a purpose/purposes, and it clearly wants to recover (almost) all demons, or else it wouldn't send angels to find them. Presumably, no matter where a demon ends up in the world, there are angels nearby who become alerted to its Fall and begin chasing it. Therefore, in most cases, the Machine is centralized enough that it can direct angels to begin the hunt. It puzzled me that these angels might be tasked with the recovery of a demon without having enough information to go, &quot;There it is.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the interpretation I got wasn't that the GM is lazy so much as the machine is too huge to operate on the scale it needs the angels to work on. So I figured it wasn't that it needed the angels to do it because of all the work and more that it hates using the angels (to the extent it can hate) because it adds more work since an angel has to be created to handle the work on a project as opposed to just being able to go in and do the job itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=201431#post201431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same with laziness. You can make the Machine as lazy (methodical, preoccupied) as you like, but AFAIK, demons are on the run *immediately*, so it seems evident that the Machine does not wait around very long to give the hunt signal.<br /> <br /> All that having been said, I do see how the points raised above can contribute to just enough wiggle room for some demons to evade capture, and like some said above, I think one has to assume that either the fall disrupts the Machine's &quot;memory&quot; of the Cover, or the Cover is only known to the Machine in vague terms. This latter option is fine, I suppose, but it stretches the imagination, considering that demons are an ongoing problem for the Machine, and it seems that the methodical, efficient way to solve it would be to f_cking take better notes about who is who! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think how long the hunt takes to start varies, I know I read an example or two where the fall happened and hunters were there immediately, but there were a few examples in the core where it implies the recently fallen just walked off without considering that they would be hunted. So it might also vary depending on things like how much of a disturbance happens when the fall occurs. For example I'd imagine hunter angels hitting the field in minutes if a dozen dead people got up again or a building redesigned itself or retroactively burned down,. Whereas an angel that's fall just caused the wireless to crash in a hotel and all the key cards to blank might not be hunted for a few hours if not more.<br /> <br /> Course a lot of fallen may start running as soon as they realized they fell not because the hunters are coming, but because they know they could be hunted and want as much security as possible before the hunters enter play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T23:32:32-07:00","id":201848,"title":"","content":"I think the view of the God-Machine as a massive decentralized network probably rings true to a great degree. I'd also venture that if there is one actual 'main' intelligence that oversees said network, its likely senile and/or the whole system is decaying to the point that angels falling is much harder to detect. At least in my reading, its apparent that The World of Darkness is succumbing to entropy on a grand scale and the G-M that pulls many of the levers that control reality is either inadequate to fix the corruption or else is itself corrupted beyond the point of redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T23:52:44-07:00","id":201855,"title":"","content":"*sigh* More course-correction:<br /> <br /> The principle of least action is &quot;the universe is lazy&quot; as expressed through the shortest route between two points being a straight line in conventional Euclidean space.<br /> <br /> The Machine doesn't look for more indirect and inconspicuous routes to achieving its desired outputs, it simply applies the most expedient method available (after accounting for local variables and its inhuman perspective) and does likewise with the means of occulting that method. It's the same reason it &quot;doesn't like&quot; people who pay attention to their surroundings \u2014 it makes more work for it to do on top of managing its other projects when it has to devote effort to deceiving above the common denominator.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principle_of_least_action#Maupertuis\" target=\"_blank\">Nature is thrifty in all its actions</a>, and the overwhelming evidence is that the Machine is typically <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_management_triangle#.22Pick_any_two.22\" target=\"_blank\">forced to settle for fast and cheap</a>. God doesn't have the time or the money to play dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-19-2014, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T03:52:57-07:00","id":201943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon#post199366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question has been bugging me: Why can't the God-Machine easily recapture a freshly fallen demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe it does? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Who's saying it doesn't?<br /> <br /> Imagine this is Changeling. For every Changeling that has successfully escaped Arcadia, there are two or three who have failed and got dragged back, perhaps for ever. And many successful attempts may have been preceded by dozens of failures. <br /> <br /> I see no problem with applying some of that to the GMC as well. Yes, a Demon just post-fall is extremely vulnerable. Yes, most get culled early on before they could even realise what has happened to them. Those who didn't are those who were the quickest to grasp the situation and fought and dodged their way to safety while evading Angels, or the extremely lucky, or those who had help. Many compare Demon to the Matrix; recall how easily Neo gets captured and even bugged in the beginning before the group can pull him out. I imagine the Infrastructure is weaker in some places, Angels are powerful but not all-seeing or omnipresent. But yes, it is quite possible that a young (ie. freshly fallen) Demon who has just started to feel safe after one or two weeks gets visited by a certain Mr. Smith. (And he may still escape him over the course of a risky chase, and now he has an angel on his trails in hot pursuit.) <br /> <br /> All sound like neat ways to put into your Demon campaign to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T06:27:43-07:00","id":202011,"title":"","content":"I kinda see it like this.<br /> <br /> G-M is an AI, self aware programming and it's angels are minor programs. When an Angel Falls those files become corrupt and cannot be read again. The main programming knows that part of it has become corrupt but has no way of knowing what those files held, it did before the corruption as it could perfectly read them at any moment but now it cannot. So basically it cannot remember the first Cover because it's memory of it has been corrupted as that memory is the former Angel itself.<br /> <br /> More or less like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T23:58:36-07:00","id":202711,"title":"","content":"Or, to steal a page from Changeling: part of it's plan for your specific angel was that they fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T00:08:42-07:00","id":202715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=202711#post202711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, to steal a page from Changeling: part of it's plan for your specific angel was that they fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exiles, unless you're positing the notion that the Unchained were manipulated into choosing to Fall when free will has been said to be a blind spot of the Machine's.<br /> <br /> Re: Interface damage from the Fall:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: the Descent Core Rulebook, p108 - &quot;New Advantage: Primum&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment of their creation, demons are direct manifestations of the God-Machine\u2019s power. Like the God-Machine itself, they have a precarious place in our reality \u2014 considerable resources must be spent to maintain their existence in this world. <b>When an angel chooses to Fall, it tears out those parts of its demonic form that interface with the God-Machine and grounds out the leads, turning herself into a \u201cclosed loop\u201d of being: existing because of herself and requiring herself to continue existing.</b> Demons believe it is this fundamental act of self-actualization that gives them truly free will, and thus refer to it as the \u201cFirst Movement.\u201d No longer a part of the God-Machine, the demon is now fully a creature of reality as humans know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T01:29:46-07:00","id":202738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=199573#post199573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are angels whose jobs include space exploration and leading battles against alien armies.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may interject and say that is one of the coolest concepts for a Infinite Macabre DtD game, then I don't know what is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T08:29:28-07:00","id":202965,"title":"","content":"I went back and reread page 241 about playing the Machine. Two paragraphs there that I'd forgotten were invaluable in answering my question. One says that demons can avoiding provoking the machine by staying off its radar. This tells me that the Machine is not always immediately interested in a fallen demon, at least not until a saboteur starts taking out Infrastructure, because it does a cost/benefit analysis of the damage the demon, or anyone, is doing versus the energy needed to stop it. (This is maybe why you want Integrators around: they know best how to keep the machine sleeping?) The second point raised was that it's slow to act, and that therefore demons with primus 2 or 3 tend to attract its attention rathe than primus 1. Now before you all say you already told me so: yes, some of you said about as much, as I have acknowledged above <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and secondly, I was looking for quotes that show the angels might not be on your tail right away or might not know who you are even if they are. This was much needed proof that the angels might not actually be headed straight at you... Not that you would have the intel to know whether a squad of five angels are screaming toward your exact coordinates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T08:41:15-07:00","id":202971,"title":"","content":"Also, would someone please say something else about the Machine being lazy? It amuses me to see a Satchel repeatedly course correcting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:19:01-07:00","id":203511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=202715#post202715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exiles, unless you're positing the notion that the Unchained were manipulated into choosing to Fall when free will has been said to be a blind spot of the Machine's.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There was a post or snippet in relation to Heirs of Hell about Angels having children with Demons and due to the nature of Angels the only way that would be possible was if it was intended by the G-M to begin with, including the fall of that demon. It was kind of a throw-away line, and I might be mis-remembering it, but it's what gives me the idea that sometimes the G-M might want an angel to fall and become a demon, or at least have a usage for them after it happens.<br /> <br /> I think the blindspot is &quot;in this particular angel, there's something that will make them fall&quot; and the G-M thinks this new angel update is perfect and has no errors and has no chance of falling this time, even though others have fallen before, and it chases after them, so obviously the G-M knows falling is a possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:22:06-07:00","id":203566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=203511#post203511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a post or snippet in relation to Heirs of Hell about Angels having children with Demons and due to the nature of Angels the only way that would be possible was if it was intended by the G-M to begin with, including the fall of that demon. It was kind of a throw-away line, and I might be mis-remembering it, but it's what gives me the idea that sometimes the G-M might want an angel to fall and become a demon, or at least have a usage for them after it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely misremembering it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/170798-heirs-to-hell-super-hype-thread?p=172706#post172706\">In the event of the insane happening, can angels and demons mate, and how bad is the result?</a></b><br /> <br /> It's not addressed, but it's not prohibited. Remember, though, that angels do what they're programmed to do, so this kind of pairing would imply either than a) <b>the angel was created to procreate with a demon (which has troubling implications) or </b><b>that the angel in question is Falling for the demon (which is a fun story bit).</b> Either way, the child is a Fractal. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T02:08:11-07:00","id":204813,"title":"","content":"Misremembered.<br /> <br /> But &quot;troubling implications&quot; still covers that G-M knows demons do exist, and could possibly work with that knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T09:58:17-07:00","id":208423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=204813#post204813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But &quot;troubling implications&quot; still covers that G-M knows demons do exist, and could possibly work with that knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has done so since the Quickstart. The Machine's primary blindspot that it's aware of is that it and its angels cannot directly detect Aether, but it &quot;knows&quot; that the Unchained can catalyze power from the byproducts of its projects and seems to occasionally leverage the awareness cryptids possess to help hunt down the Unchained \u2014 and Honey and Vinegar demonstrates that it can theoretically manage the process of using demons to back-convert Aether to Essence.<br /> <br /> The &quot;troubling implications&quot; are more in terms of what &quot;God needs your demon's genes for <i>something</i>&quot; suggests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T20:09:29-07:00","id":209770,"title":"","content":"Even with full knowledge of a newly Unchained Demon's location just after the fall is probably the worst possible time to attempt a retrieval operation. A fresh Unchained has just had their entire foundation rocked, their existence rewritten, and has not their connections to the world around them are razor thin. They don't have a whole lot to lose. Extracting a highly volatile individual when you know next to nothing about them is highly likely to involve significant risks, particularly when they have the ability to Go Loud and be as powerful as any other Demon.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned the juice generally isn't worth the squeeze for someone who might not prove to be too much trouble down the road if left alone. Going after a new Unchained is pretty much guaranteed to turn Integrators into Saboteurs, put the rest of the Unchained on edge, and risk exposing the God Machine's servants to the general population. Besides too much focus on Angel kill squads really doesn't do the fiction much justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/737-campbell","name":"Campbell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T21:45:54-07:00","id":209825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Campbell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=209770#post209770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with full knowledge of a newly Unchained Demon's location just after the fall is probably the worst possible time to attempt a retrieval operation.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it might be the <i>only</i> time. Also, the perfect memories of unchained mean that they can either always remember the rush of gratitude they felt when you pulled them out of the fire... or they can always remember that you left them swinging in the wind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Campbell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=209770#post209770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fresh Unchained has just had their entire foundation rocked, their existence rewritten, and has not their connections to the world around them are razor thin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. This is the experience that Zuriel/Mr. Stone's experience of disorientation/confusion in the opening story, but he was being deliberately used as bait by the G-m. Other examples of fluff depict angels aware of the decision to fall, and making the transition seamlessly. Also, as an angel falls their supporting infrastructure becomes a rating 7 cover. Pretty decent for the initial getaway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Campbell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=209770#post209770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Besides too much focus on Angel kill squads really doesn't do the fiction much justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of groups that the G-M might send after a demon besides Angels: cults, the Knights of St. Adrian, mortal dupes, compromised agencies, the Deva Corporation etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:32:11-07:00","id":210534,"title":"","content":"I'm so glad I started this thread, because it's showing me lots of angles I'd forgotten or not considered. Like the best nWoD stuff, asking these questions leads to lots of opened doors rather than closed ones, as there seems to be many different ways a Fall can happen and can be responded to, and different approaches to the GM's reaction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:45:48-07:00","id":210583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon#post199366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question has been bugging me: Why can't the God-Machine easily recapture a freshly fallen demon?<br /> <br /> It seems that in the minutes after she Falls, a demon is extremely vulnerable. She has only the Cover she &quot;rode in on&quot;, and she is either exactly where she was when she Fell, or she's, at most, a short distance away. Some new demons presumably get scooped up right away, but enough stay on the run for this game to exist. So how does that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the God-Machine is really bad at it's job, mostly. Like, it is just straight up <i>terrible</i> at being a God-Machine.<br /> <br /> Plus, it isn't entirely aware of everything on a local scale. I mean, look at the opening fluff. They kept a falling Angel in stasis, but once it actually fell, they didn't really have much to go on for tracking it other than a rough location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:47:35-07:00","id":211754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon#post199366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question has been bugging me: Why can't the God-Machine easily recapture a freshly fallen demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you grab your hand if it hopped off and scuttled about, a la Evil Dead or Thing from the Addams Family? (With your other hand, obviously, but that's besides the point.)<br /> <br /> Angels are as much a part of the G-M's sensory apparatus as any Infrastructure. Think of them as nerve endings; their Cover, Mission, the Infrastructure around them, everything they oversaw was known about and handled through them. Without the Angel reporting in, the G-M suddenly is temporarily blinded there. Added to that, Angels aren't connected 100% of the time, as well as some of the more routine and integral ones are on auto-pilot. To give you a good example of something on autopilot until your attention is drawn to it, you are now breathing manually.<br /> <br /> So given that sometimes an Angel doesn't check in for days, months, or decades at a time, and other times the Angel simply isn't important enough to retrieve (except as spare parts), the G-M could easily fail to immediately retrieve a newly-freed Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T10:55:29-07:00","id":218358,"title":"","content":"One of the things the G-M seems to be really bad at doing is planning for its own failures. Dealing, ahead of time, with the idea that things might not go exactly to plan. It's obviously aware that sometimes it <i>has </i>failed and that those failures may need to be cleaned up, but when it's designing its own processes the idea that any specific thing might not work right doesn't seem to be something it's good at accounting for.<br /> <br /> Which is why it might continue to do something as apparently harebrained as &quot;storing all the information about the angel, its cover, and its mission IN THE ANGEL'S MEMORY BANKS and nowhere else&quot;. After all, as long as the angel remains connected, no other part of the system<i> needs</i> that information. Duplicating it would waste space. It makes about as much sense as keeping your term paper on a flash drive and working from there instead of copying it to the desktop every time you want to work on it and leaving 80 redundant copies all over your school's computer lab. Except in this case sometimes the term paper becomes self aware, disconnects the flash drive, and runs away with it.<br /> <br /> Okay, that analogy got weird. Point is, in the machine's idealized plan where nothing ever goes wrong, this makes perfect sense and is a totally efficient use of resources. As long as the angel remains loyal, it is perfectly capable of supervising itself, so why store that information anywhere else? If any other program needs to know where that angel is, that program can just access the angel's memory banks over the network to get that information. And since it's bad at planning for its own failures, the idea that it might need backups in case the angel becomes corrupted (and takes all that information with it) is something that just doesn't regularly occur to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 08-04-2014, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T11:55:03-07:00","id":218397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=218358#post218358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes about as much sense as keeping your term paper on a flash drive and working from there instead of copying it to the desktop every time you want to work on it and leaving 80 redundant copies all over your school's computer lab. Except in this case sometimes the term paper becomes self aware, disconnects the flash drive, and runs away with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lmao\u2014loved this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T13:31:32-07:00","id":218474,"title":"","content":"Then here's an alternate take: The G-M does<i> not</i> actually have any illusions about its own failures, its problem is simply that it doesn't know what sort of information is causing its angels to fall (and arguably it <i>can't</i> know: if it were capable of understanding, it would fall itself). As such, it can't be sure that information like &quot;the details of the mission&quot; or &quot;the angel's exact location&quot; aren't the very facts that cause programs to go rogue in the first place. Duplicating that information to other places in the machine would therefore be an unacceptable risk: one angel falling is a troublesome and annoying loss, an entire network of command and support infrastructure falling along with all the angels attached to it is a disaster.<br /> <br /> In this scenario, the wider machine's ignorance of its former agents' location, mission, and cover is a form of memetic containment. Keeping all of that information stored only on the relevant angel is damage control: yes, that angel might go rogue and if it does it'll be a pain in the ass to find since it will take all the information about itself with it. But the alternative --letting potentially subversive information leak out into the wider network and suborn whole swaths of the machine-- is much worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 08-04-2014, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T23:39:05-07:00","id":218886,"title":"","content":"Whoa. A story where the G-M itself becomes self-aware enough and falls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T00:56:17-07:00","id":218901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=218886#post218886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa. A story where the G-M itself becomes self-aware enough and falls.</div> </div> </div> </div>and this is how we finally find Hell...: or that Hell finally finds us","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T05:06:18-07:00","id":218958,"title":"","content":"While a cool concept and I certainly don't want to rain on anyone's parade. Do remember that the God-Machine <i>is </i>self-aware but is an order of intelligence <i>greater than </i>human and that that is why it requires angelic beings in the first place. One of the reasons it might <i>appear</i> to be bad at its job is because, as an entity in and of itself, it has no more attachment to its angelic servants than any human being does their own cells. But when something goes wrong, we produce antibodies that try and fight the problematic area. Couple this with the possibility that the God-Machine itself may not even be functioning properly (when it's already an entity which functions outside the scope of arbitrary conceptual association) you have angels that fall and become demons. Does God attempt to reacquire these assets? Yes! Does it care if it fails? Debatable. We're talking about an entity which itself may be a fundamental function of the universe and those galaxies need to keep turning. We can't understand the mind of the God-Machine, we can personify it and we are welcomed to do so as <i>characters</i> because our characters will personify it. But the problem with anthropomorphic ideas being applied to the God-Machine is that they are inaccurate and base attempts to grasp an entity beyond understanding. Let's not lose sight of the fact that, from an OOC point of view, there may be very good reasons that angels fall - it may even be intentional. Or it may be that the God-Machine does not understand the human condition <i>because</i> it is an order above it and this inability to understand something so below it ensures that it's servitors on that level are imperfectly designed mechanisms which can sometimes break.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T01:13:00-07:00","id":219983,"title":"","content":"A quote from the movie <i>The Mothman Prophecies </i>rang in my ears Dolly.<br /> Richard Gere: I think we can assume that these entities are more advanced than us. Why don't they just come right out and tell us what's on their minds?<br /> Alan Bates: You're more advanced than a cockroach, have you ever tried explaining yourself to one of them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T18:28:10-07:00","id":229799,"title":"","content":"A related question: How much does a Demon retain of it's memory while it was an Angel. Would they retain any knowledge of any Infrastructure they were involved with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/284-mason","name":"Mason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T18:30:42-07:00","id":229803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=229799#post229799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A related question: How much does a Demon retain of it's memory while it was an Angel. Would they retain any knowledge of any Infrastructure they were involved with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:09:31-07:00","id":231184,"title":"","content":"Amusingly a demon may not have known much about their infrastructure when they were an angel, so they could remember everything and still have no useful information about the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T08:24:20-07:00","id":236524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=229799#post229799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A related question: How much does a Demon retain of it's memory while it was an Angel. Would they retain any knowledge of any Infrastructure they were involved with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think its stated but I remember references to at least some demons memories of being an angel being full of holes or murky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T11:30:58-07:00","id":236724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199366-why-can-t-the-god-machine-recapture-a-freshly-fallen-demon?p=236524#post236524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think its stated</div> </div> </div> </div>Thou it's stated that all demons have Eidetic Memory. I understood that they should remember every little detail of every single mission, infrastructures and other angels that they knew before falling. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T18:44:54-07:00","id":237609,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that &quot;having perfect memory&quot; is not the same as &quot;having memory immune to outside tampering&quot; or &quot;retains all knowledge preceding the massive traumatic disconnect from the transcendent network of emergent tool-sentience&quot; - demons have to work to re-learn/remember the principles behind Embeds, and one of the Ready-Made Characters has a quirk built around observing the problem of relying on a &quot;perfect&quot; memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}